    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look for high-volume production tonight, headlined by **Kyle Tucker** (82.17) and **Andy Pages** (72.96), who both benefit immensely from a favorable encounter with Randy V\u00e1squez. Both outfielders carry the \"Wind Out\" bonus, boosting their power profiles, and their scoring is further bolstered by the soft SP_xERA of 4.76. Joining them in the high-ceiling tier is **Jackson Merrill** (72.01), whose dynamic platoon advantage against Roki Sasaki makes him a mandatory start despite the opponent's pedigree. **Sam Antonacci** (65.19) remains a foundational piece of our lineup today; his leadoff duties combined with a plus matchup against Cecconi make him our most efficient MI option, providing a vital bridge to our power hitters.\n\nConversely, we are exercising caution with **Josh Lowe** (43.62), who survives the lineup cut only by the skin of his teeth due to his elite speed profile and a dynamic platoon boost. He faces a daunting challenge against Miller, whose 2.42 xERA is the most restrictive on the slate, forcing us to prioritize his contribution to the scarce SB category over his lower raw output. On the bench, **Nolan Schanuel** (39.91) was the clear odd man out; he fell just short of our 40-point threshold for active duty, largely due to the severe SP Skill penalty associated with the Miller matchup. While **Schanuel** represents a consistent floor, the lack of a platoon edge and the unfavorable park factors rendered him a liability compared to the upside offered by **Liam Hicks** (57.76), who leverages a significant park factor adjustment to maintain his UTIL spot.\n\nWe are operating with \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Tucker**, **Pages**, and **Merrill**, meaning their projected slotting is subject to change; should any of these core pieces move down in the order, their efficiency scores will require immediate re-evaluation. While **Jordan Westburg** remains on the IL, our current configuration balances the necessity of elite sprint speed with the reality of today's difficult pitching matchups. We will lean on the offensive synergy between **Miguel Vargas** and **Antonacci** at the top of the order to catalyze runs, while relying on the wind-aided profiles of our primary outfielders to clear the fences.",
